WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.588
A lock-free index

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.378
that still does

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.274
range scans

00:00:03.798 --> 00:00:05.295
Researchers from UT

00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:06.639
Austin and ETH

00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:07.677
Zurich built Arctic

00:00:07.855 --> 00:00:09.128
a lock-free adaptive

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.859
radix tree

00:00:09.998 --> 00:00:10.929
They say no

00:00:10.741 --> 00:00:12.085
index before offered

00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:12.969
high performance

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.302
lock freedom and

00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:15.599
range scans together

00:00:16.126 --> 00:00:17.871
A freezing-based coordination

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:18.814
protocol keeps it

00:00:18.626 --> 00:00:19.510
non-blocking

00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:20.288
and a new

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.220
memory reclamation

00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:22.470
scheme uses operation

00:00:22.282 --> 00:00:23.708
keys to approximate

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.663
reachable pointers

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.121
Swapped in for

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:27.206
the default skiplists

00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:28.409
it raised write-heavy

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:29.128
throughput by up

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.284
to 40 percent in

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.053
RocksDB and 12 percent

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.654
in Turso

00:00:33.174 --> 00:00:34.188
Full story on

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:34.895
the dashboard
